/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (The Expression Tree Generator and Evaluator is a Python-based project designed to construct and evaluate arithmetic expressions using a tree data structure. An expression tree is a binary tree in which the leaf nodes represent operands, such as numbers, and the internal nodes represent operators, such as addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division. This project helps users understand how arithmetic expressions can be represented in the form of a tree and evaluated efficiently.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (The project accepts an arithmetic expression as input, processes the expression, and generates its corresponding expression tree. It then evaluates the expression using tree traversal and recursive functions. The system helps reduce errors in manual calculations and makes it easier to understand the order of operations in complex expressions.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
